tags: build, build_mu

A rate of the node: the price of one build of a service that the node does not have built.

The value is MU for one. Example: 1000000. The node takes it from the balance that
pays for the action.

The rate has no scope. A reader that does not know the rate ignores it.

=== formal
base=one
class=rate
name=build
of=the build of the container of a service that the node did not build before; 0 for a service that it has built
scope=none
